Leetcode - 860

Logic :

Initialise five , ten and twenty 
traverse the array in for loop using num variable
if the num equal to 5 , then increment variable five
else if the num equal to 10 , then check whether you can able to give five rupee change , i.e., five should not be positive. if yes , decrement five and increment 10 , else return false
else , (balance should be 15)
    check whether you have ten and five rupee denomination , then decrement five and ten.   
    else check whether you have atleast 3 five rupee denomination , then reduce five to 3 times
    else return false
if for loop iterates fully , it indicates , there is sufficient amount of changes possible , so return true

Code :

class Solution {
    public boolean lemonadeChange(int[] bills) {
        int five=0;
        int ten=0;
        int twenty=0;
        for(int num:bills){
            if(num==5){
                five++;
            }
            else if(num==10){
                if(five<=0){
                    return false;
                }
                five--;
                ten++;
            }
            else{
                if(ten>0 && five>0){
                    ten--;
                    five--;
                }
                else if(five>2){
                    five-=3;
                }
                else{
                    return false;
                }
            }
            
        }
        return true;
    }
}
